Subject: A high-fidelity, photorealistic UI design for "RocketRecap.com" with a "Whimsical Cottagecore & Nature" aesthetic.

Composition & Layout:

The Environment (The Map of YouTube):

Concept: Visualize the "Neural Latent Space" as a magical, top-down view of a forest floor at twilight.

The Data: Instead of stars, thousands of tiny bioluminescent mushrooms and glowing fireflies represent the videos.

Connections: Faint, glowing blue "mycelium threads" (fungal roots) connect the mushrooms, representing the hidden connections between topics.

Clusters: Distinct groves of moss represent topic clusters. Label them with wooden signposts sticking out of the moss: "Science," "History," and "Music."

The Interface (Foreground):

Container: A polished, live-edge oak wood board resting gently on the mossy ground, serving as the main control panel.

Header: The text "RocketRecap" carved deeply into the top of the wood, filled with gold paint.

Input Section: Two rectangular indents in the wood lined with cream-colored parchment paper.

Left Parchment: "Paste Video Link."

Right Parchment: "Paste Text."

Button: A large, round, glowing Amber Gemstone embedded in the wood with the word "SUMMARIZE" floating inside it.

The "Local Neighborhood" Widget:

To the right of the wooden board, place a brass vintage magnifying glass lying on the moss.

Visual Function: Through the glass lens, we see a magnified view of a specific cluster of glowing mushrooms, highlighting the "Current Video" and its immediate neighbors.

Lighting & Atmosphere: Magical twilight lighting. The primary light comes from the glowing mushrooms and the amber button. Soft shadows, rich textures of wood grain, moss, and brass.

Style: 8k resolution, magical realism, UI design, tactile textures, Studio Ghibli meets high-end web design.